sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ha02-24> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Horned quadrupeds that lack a full set of teeth in both jaws have a stomach of four chambers, and these are the animals that chew the cud.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Horned animals lacking upper front teeth have four stomachs and ruminate";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, The History of Animals (Historia Animalium), Book II, Part 17; translated by D'Arcy Wentworth Thompson, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. IV (1910). Scope: Horned ruminants (cattle, sheep, goats, deer)"
}
